---
/**
 * hospitality / PageBI — "Palm Hour" (hotels, villas & short stays).
 *
 * Terracotta & lagoon shade: Fraunces display over Figtree body with DM Mono
 * labels, on sun-warmed plaster, alternating into a deep lagoon-green "shade"
 * band. The warm ground and the shade bands exist to FLATTER an owner's phone
 * photography rather than expose it — that is the whole art direction, and it is
 * why every photo lives in an inset `.plate` frame with a paper mat rather than
 * bleeding full-width.
 *
 * ROLE OF THIS FILE: the wrapper emits the WHOLE document (doctype, <head>,
 * tokens, fonts, Leaflet boot, skip link, scroll-reveal). It does NOT compose
 * with BaseLayout. It is the only file in the family that touches `siteData`;
 * the 15 section components receive only `layout` + `content`.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS OWNED BY THIS FILE: none. PageBI renders no editable text of
 * its own — it only READS layout.businessName / layout.tagline (<title>),
 * content.description (<meta name="description">), layout.favicon (<link
 * rel="icon">) and layout.ogImage || layout.favicon (og:image). Every
 * data-field / data-image-field / data-href-field hook lives in a section
 * component. Section visibility is the 13 camelCase `visibility.*` keys below,
 * every one tested `!== false` (undefined ⇒ render).
 *
 * DESIGN ISOLATION: every selector in the global block is prefixed
 * `html[data-page="BI"]`, including the `*` reset, `body`, `img`, `a`,
 * `::selection` and the base primitives, so nothing leaks into a sister wrapper
 * built in the same run — and nothing leaks in.
 *
 * THEMING: the native palette is emitted FIRST and the engine's
 * `html:root{…!important}` block LAST in <head>, which is the only reason an
 * explicit admin colour pick wins the cascade. Never move it above the design
 * <style is:global> or above the {__fontHref} link.
 *
 * FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL (two lines, wrapper-local, touches no shared file):
 * lib/astro-builder.ts defaults `layout.fontPairing` to the literal 'modern',
 * and resolveTheme's `lockVariant` only blanks ''/'auto'/'default' — so without
 * the sentinel buildOverrideCss force-swaps Space Grotesk + Inter with
 * !important on ~every real site and Fraunces never reaches a visitor. We treat
 * astro-builder's DEFAULT as unset; a deliberate admin pick still applies.
 *
 * FORBIDDEN CLASS NAMES in this family (none of these is inferable — read
 * lib/genericThemeOverrides.ts before adding a button anywhere):
 *   .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta .nav-right .testi
 *   and `.hero` on a <section> (the engine force-paints `.hero .btn-ghost`
 *   white-on-transparent, which would strand a white label on this light hero;
 *   the arrival section is therefore class="arrival").
 * This family's buttons are `.btn--fill` / `.btn--line` / `.linkc` (double
 * dash) on purpose: they dodge the engine's `.btn-primary{color:<on-primary>
 * !important}` pin, which is sub-AA in 6 of 13 schemes. There is ZERO
 * !important in this template outside the reduced-motion reveal reset — the
 * rename removes the fight instead of winning it.
 * TWO names are REQUIRED and deliberate: the stat rail IS class="trust" and the
 * closing band IS class="cta-band", because in both places the engine's on-ink
 * label pin is CORRECT (both sit on an ink fill, and pickOn(ink) flips with ink
 * — 9.11:1 in the worst of the 13 schemes).
 *
 * KNOWN LIMITATIONS, recorded rather than fixed (fixing any of them needs a
 * shared-file change, which is out of scope here):
 *  1. components/editor/editorBridge.ts resolves a section by the FIRST
 *     [data-field^="<prefix>."] in document order. HeaderBI's wordmark carries
 *     `footer.brand` and its CTA pill carries `hero.cta1.text`, so toggling
 *     FOOTER or HERO off in the editor hides the HEADER. Family-wide; the
 *     alternatives either invent a content key (R7) or make the brand
 *     un-editable (R1).
 *  2. components/editor/genericContentSchema.ts declares `location.hours` as a
 *     single TEXT field, so LocationBI's Array.isArray(loc.hours) always falls
 *     through to content.footer.hours while still emitting
 *     data-field="location.hours.N.day". That path does not match
 *     SandboxEditorV2's SKIP regex, so a first inline edit would create a fresh
 *     location.hours array and orphan the remaining footer rows.
 *  3. ctaBand cta2/cta3 LABELS are effectively fixed (no sidebar form field, and
 *     the inline editor returns early on any element carrying data-href-field),
 *     which is why the closing band is designed to work fully with cta1 alone.
 *  4. services.items[].price / .duration / .tag are not in
 *     genericContentSchema's services row (title/desc/note/image), so the
 *     per-night RATE is currently unreachable from the admin. ServicesBI handles
 *     that honestly — `anyPrice` suppresses the rate column AND its header row
 *     together — but the commercial value only lands once those three fields are
 *     added to the row schema. Filed, not fixed (R7).
 *  5. Derived headlines read generic on a hotel ('Services we provide' over the
 *     room ledger, 'A look at our work' over the lookbook). mergeShallow makes
 *     the derived layer authoritative, so a .astro fallback there is dead code —
 *     the admin edits services.headline / gallery.headline / why.headline.
 *
 * RENDER ORDER is deliberate and NOT the family norm: rooms → amenities →
 * gallery come BEFORE the story, because in this vertical photography and the
 * tariff are the product. Do not "restore" the gallery to a late slot.
 *
 * Leaflet: this wrapper defines window.__hospitalityBIInitMap (family-unique) and
 * LocationBI calls that exact string. Keep `el.innerHTML = ''` in the boot — it
 * is what erases the drawn fallback map-face — and keep id="map" literal.
 */
import HeaderBI from './header/HeaderBI.astro';
import HeroBI from './hero/HeroBI.astro';
import TrustBI from './trust/TrustBI.astro';
import ServicesBI from './services/ServicesBI.astro';
import WhyBI from './why/WhyBI.astro';
import GalleryBI from './gallery/GalleryBI.astro';
import AboutBI from './about/AboutBI.astro';
import HowBI from './how/HowBI.astro';
import TestimonialsBI from './testimonials/TestimonialsBI.astro';
import FaqBI from './faq/FaqBI.astro';
import AreaBI from './area/AreaBI.astro';
import CredentialsBI from './credentials/CredentialsBI.astro';
import LocationBI from './location/LocationBI.astro';
import CtaBandBI from './ctaBand/CtaBandBI.astro';
import FooterBI from './footer/FooterBI.astro';
import { resolveTheme, buildFontHref, buildOverrideCss } from '../../lib/genericThemeOverrides';

interface Props { siteData: any; }
const { siteData } = Astro.props;
const layout = siteData.layout ?? {};
const content = siteData.content ?? {};
const visibility = siteData.visibility ?? {};
const title = layout.businessName
  ? `${layout.businessName}${layout.tagline ? ' — ' + layout.tagline : ''}`
  : 'Welcome';
const { scheme: __themeScheme, pairing: __resolvedPairing } = resolveTheme(layout, (content as any).business_type, { lockVariant: true });
// 'modern' is astro-builder's DEFAULT, not a choice (lib/astro-builder.ts).
// Treating it as unset keeps Fraunces; any deliberate admin pick still applies.
const __themePairing = __resolvedPairing === 'modern' ? '' : __resolvedPairing;
const __overrideCss = buildOverrideCss(__themeScheme, __themePairing);
const __fontHref = buildFontHref(__themePairing);
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-page="BI">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  {content.description && <meta name="description" content={content.description} />}
  <!-- Browser-chrome tint. A <meta> cannot read a CSS var, so this duplicates
       the plaster ground token (--paper) that the sticky header sits on. -->
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#F6EBDC" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="" />
  <!-- Palm Hour native fonts: Fraunces (variable, SOFT + WONK axes) display,
       Figtree body, DM Mono labels. Always loaded so the variant reads as
       designed even when the admin never touched the font dropdown.
       FALLBACK, swap in wholesale if the multi-axis tuple ever 400s (one bad
       tuple kills all three families):
       https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,500;9..144,700;9..144,800&family=Figtree:wght@400;500;600;700&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap -->
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght,SOFT,WONK@9..144,300..800,0..100,0..1&family=Figtree:wght@400;500;600;700&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
  {layout.favicon && <link rel="icon" href={layout.favicon} />}
  {(layout.ogImage || layout.favicon) && <meta property="og:image" content={layout.ogImage || layout.favicon} />}

  <style is:global>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       PageBI · "Palm Hour" — hospitality (hotels / villas / short stays).
       Tokens + shared base primitives. EVERY selector is prefixed
       html[data-page="BI"] so nothing leaks into a sister wrapper, or in.

       FIVE LOAD-BEARING FACTS. Do not "tidy" any of them:

       1. R6 / SPECIFICITY. Every appearance-bearing base primitive is wrapped in
          :where() -> (0,1,1), so an Astro-scoped single-compound section rule
          (0,2,0) wins. Removing a :where() is the documented cause of every photo
          frame collapsing to the base height (squished band). BELT AND BRACES:
          sections also size .plate with an INLINE style="aspect-ratio:X;min-height:0"
          — inline outranks every selector, so the specificity argument never has
          to be won per section.

       2. BUTTON CLASS NAMES. .btn--fill / .btn--line / .linkc, double-dash, on
          purpose. They dodge buildOverrideCss's
          `.btn-primary,…{color:<on-primary>!important}` (sub-AA in 6 of 13
          schemes) and `.hero .btn-ghost{color:#FFF!important;background:transparent
          !important}` (which would strand a white label on this light hero).
          NEVER use in this family: .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light
          .nav-cta .nav-right .testi .cta-band. NEVER put a .btn--line inside
          .cta-band or footer — EVERY .btn label there is pinned to --on-ink, so a
          transparent fill would strand it. Use .linkc. There is NO !important
          reclaim war anywhere in this template: the rename removes the fight.

       3. HOVER. Never changes hue, never goes light or transparent. An inset
          rgba(0,0,0,.16) darkens only the fill (it paints above the background and
          below the label). Label on the darkened fill: 13.07 native, 10.04 worst
          (green), 11.83 (maroon, where --ink is the light token).

       4. FOCUS. One DUO ring for everything: a 3px var(--paper) outline inside a
          6px var(--ink) halo. Built from the ink/paper pair, so on a light ground
          the ink halo separates the ring from the page (>=8.40 in all 13 schemes)
          and on a shade ground the paper ring separates from the halo (same pair).
          This replaces outline:currentColor, which measured 1.00:1 on a filled
          button (paper ring on paper ground) in every scheme.

       5. HEAD ORDER. This block must be followed by
          {__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />} and then, as
          the LAST node in the head, a global style node fed set:html={__overrideCss}.
          The engine's html:root{…!important} only beats these tokens because it
          comes later in source order.
          (Never write a literal closing style/script tag inside this block — it is
          an HTML raw-text element, so the parser would end the stylesheet here.)
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    html[data-page="BI"] {
      /* grounds — sun-warmed plaster / linen / woven sand */
      --paper: #F6EBDC;
      --paper-2: #FDF7EE;
      --card: #EDDFC9;
      /* shade — the deep lagoon-green ground behind every inverted band */
      --ink: #12312C;
      --ink-soft: #3F5A4F;
      --line: #DCC7AA;
      /* warmth — terracotta primary, burnt clay, mango light (NEVER text) */
      --accent: #BD5028;
      --accent-deep: #8E3517;
      --accent-light: #E9A03C;
      --muted: #6E5B47;
      /* rgb triplets for token-driven tints (all remapped by buildOverrideCss) */
      --paper-rgb: 246,235,220;
      --ink-rgb: 18,49,44;
      --accent-rgb: 189,80,40;
      /* contrast aliases the override engine + inherited rules expect */
      --on-ink: #F6EBDC;
      --on-paper: #12312C;
      --on-accent: #FFFFFF;
      --on-primary: #FFFFFF;
      /* type + metrics */
      --disp: "Fraunces", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --serif: "Fraunces", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --sans: "Figtree", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --mono: "DM Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      --maxw: 1240px;
      --r-lg: 26px;
      --r-md: 18px;
      --r-sm: 12px;
    }

    /* VERIFIED CONTRAST (sRGB relative luminance):
       ink/paper 11.88 · ink/paper-2 13.13 · ink/card 10.66
       ink-soft/paper 6.40 · /paper-2 7.07 · /card 5.74 · /card+weave(#E2D6C1) 5.25
       muted/paper 5.49 · /paper-2 6.07 · /card 4.92 (tightest light pair)
       paper on ink 11.88 · rgba(paper,.86)=#D6D1C3 9.17 · .78=#C4C2B5 7.81
       .74=#BBBBAE 7.21 · .60=#9BA196 5.28
       ink on rgba(accent,.16)/paper = #EDD2BF 9.71 · over card #E5C8AF 8.80
       paper on rgba(accent,.16)/ink = #2D362B 10.65
       caption pill: paper on OPAQUE ink 11.88 over ANY photo
       BANNED, recorded as evidence: accent-as-text/paper 4.11 · accent-light 1.87 ·
       engine accent-deep on maroon paper 1.29 · engine accent-light on dark ink 2.43
       WORST OF 13 SCHEMES: ink/paper 8.40 (green) · pinned on-ink on ink 9.11 (green) ·
       our paper label on the 16%-darkened hover fill 10.04 (green) / 11.83 (maroon) ·
       .btn--line hover rgba(paper,.14) on shade 5.87 (green) ·
       ink-soft/card 4.95 (dark). NOTHING carrying text is below 4.5:1. */

    /* ── reset + document ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BI"] *,
    html[data-page="BI"] *::before,
    html[data-page="BI"] *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html[data-page="BI"] { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BI"] { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
    html[data-page="BI"] body {
      margin: 0; padding: 0;
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.68;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden;
      /* faint linen tooth on the plaster ground — token-driven, so it recolours */
      background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.022) 0 1px, transparent 1px 5px);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] img { max-width: 100%; display: block; }
    html[data-page="BI"] a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    html[data-page="BI"] ::selection { background: rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.28); color: var(--ink); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--disp); color: var(--ink);
      font-optical-sizing: auto; letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1.06;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(h1) { font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 45, "WONK" 1; }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(h3,h4) { font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 35, "WONK" 0; }
    /* This bare-element paragraph reset is (0,1,1): always qualify a section's own
       paragraph rules with a parent class (.about-prose p) so they out-specify it. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(p) { margin: 0 0 1em; }

    /* ── layout scaffolding ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.wrap) { width: min(var(--maxw), 92vw); margin-inline: auto; }
    html[data-page="BI"] section { padding: clamp(76px,9vw,128px) 0; position: relative; }

    /* ── BAND GROUNDS. Four, and only four. Sections pick one by name.
          Default (no class) = plaster --paper. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-linen) { background-color: var(--paper-2); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-sand)  { background-color: var(--card); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) { background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .h2 { color: var(--paper); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .body,
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .lede { color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.86); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .sec-head { color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.74); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .sec-head .sh-rule {
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent-light), rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.20));
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .plate { border-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.16); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .plate.mat { border-color: var(--ink); }

    /* ── .kick — eyebrow. Mono label preceded by a decorative terracotta lozenge.
          The label text is --muted (5.49 on paper); the colour hit is the ::before,
          which carries no text. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.kick) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px;
      font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; font-size: 10.5px;
      letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.kick)::before {
      content: ""; flex: 0 0 auto; width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 2px;
      background: var(--accent); transform: rotate(45deg);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .kick { color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.74); }

    /* ── .sec-head — literal WORD label · warm hairline · data tag.
          .sh-l is a design literal describing the TEMPLATE. It is a WORD, never a
          number: every section self-hides when empty, so numbered eyebrows render a
          ledger with visible gaps on a sparse site. .sh-r is the ONLY data slot and
          must come from <sec>.tag — a hardcoded right-hand line is a fabrication. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.sec-head) {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: clamp(12px,2vw,22px);
      margin: 0 0 clamp(30px,4vw,52px);
      font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.sec-head) .sh-rule {
      flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 24px; height: 1px; opacity: .85;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), var(--line));
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.sec-head) .sh-r { text-align: right; }

    /* ── display headline + UNDERLINE emphasis.
          Emphasis is an underline, never a colour swap: accent-as-text is 4.11 and
          the engine's --accent-deep collapses to 1.29 under maroon. The text keeps
          `inherit` — ink on light bands, paper on .band-shade. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.h2) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(34px,4.8vw,66px);
      line-height: 1.0; letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 0 0 .34em;
      color: var(--ink); max-width: 24ch;
      font-optical-sizing: auto; font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 45, "WONK" 1;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.h2 em),
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.h2 .em),
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.uline) {
      font-style: normal; color: inherit;
      background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.55), rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.55));
      background-repeat: no-repeat; background-size: 100% .16em; background-position: 0 92%;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.body) {
      color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(15.5px,1.4vw,17.5px); line-height: 1.74;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.lede) {
      color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(16px,1.5vw,18.5px); line-height: 1.72;
      max-width: 46ch; margin: 0;
    }
    /* ── .mono — small mono meta on a light ground (--muted, 4.92 worst: on card) */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.mono) {
      font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; font-size: 10.5px;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .mono { color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.74); }
    /* ── .fig — the tabular money/stat figure. tabular-nums survives a font swap. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.fig) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink);
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums; letter-spacing: -.01em;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .fig { color: var(--paper); }

    /* ── BUTTONS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       Proven pairs (native / worst of 13):
         .btn--fill            paper on ink                    11.88 / 8.40
         .btn--fill:hover      paper on ink+16% black          13.07 / 10.04
         .btn--fill pinned     on-ink on ink (cta-band/footer) 11.88 / 9.11
         .btn--line            ink on paper                    11.88 / 8.40
         .btn--line:hover      paper on ink                    11.88 / 8.40
         .btn--line on shade   paper on ink                    11.88 / 8.40
         ..:hover on shade     paper on rgba(paper,.14)/ink     8.01 / 5.87
         .linkc                ink on card/paper (never changes on hover) 10.66 / 8.40
       No fill is ever a mid-tone: every one is the darkest or the lightest token. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.btn) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .55em;
      padding: 15px 28px; min-height: 48px;
      border-radius: 999px; border: 1.5px solid transparent;
      font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; font-size: 11.5px;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; text-decoration: none;
      cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;
      transition: background-color .18s ease, box-shadow .18s ease, transform .18s ease, border-color .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.btn--fill) {
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--ink);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.btn--fill:hover) {
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--ink);
      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 999px rgba(0,0,0,.16), 0 0 0 4px rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.30);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.btn--fill:active) { transform: translateY(0); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.btn--line) {
      background-color: transparent; color: var(--ink); border-color: rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.55);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.btn--line:hover) {
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--ink);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.btn--line:active) { transform: translateY(0); }
    /* .btn--line INSIDE a shade band inverts. Declared here once, globally, so no
       section has to restate it. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .btn--line {
      color: var(--paper); border-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.5);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .btn--line:hover {
      background-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.14); color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--paper);
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page="BI"] .btn { transition: none; }
      html[data-page="BI"] .btn--fill:hover,
      html[data-page="BI"] .btn--line:hover { transform: none; }
    }

    /* ── .linkc — quiet text-link action. Used INSTEAD of a second button inside
          .cta-band / footer, because it carries no .btn class and so is never
          touched by the engine's on-ink label pin. Colour never changes on hover
          (only the accent underline thickens), so it cannot fail. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.linkc) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .5em; min-height: 44px;
      font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; font-size: 11.5px;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-bottom: 3px;
      transition: border-bottom-width .18s ease, border-bottom-color .18s ease, transform .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.linkc:hover) {
      color: var(--ink); border-bottom-width: 3px; border-bottom-color: var(--accent-deep);
      transform: translateY(-1px);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .linkc { color: var(--paper); border-bottom-color: var(--accent-light); }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BI"] .linkc { transition: none; } }

    /* ── FOCUS · the DUO ring. See load-bearing fact 4. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(a,button,summary,[tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--paper); outline-offset: 0;
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--ink);
      border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.btn):focus-visible,
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.linkc):focus-visible { border-radius: 999px; }

    /* ── .plate — THE photo frame. Every image in the template is one of these.
          Sections size it with an inline style="aspect-ratio:X;min-height:0".
          The fallback gradient is token-built, so it recolours with the scheme. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.plate) {
      position: relative; overflow: hidden; border-radius: var(--r-lg);
      background-color: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); isolation: isolate;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.plate) .ph {
      position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1;
      background-color: var(--card);
      background-size: cover; background-position: center; background-repeat: no-repeat;
      background-image:
        radial-gradient(78% 64% at 24% 16%, rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.30), transparent 62%),
        radial-gradient(66% 60% at 84% 90%, rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.28), transparent 60%),
        repeating-linear-gradient(48deg, rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.05) 0 1px, transparent 1px 7px);
      transition: transform .5s ease;
    }
    /* .cap — caption on an OPAQUE ink pill, never a gradient scrim: 11.88 over ANY
       owner photo, however dark or blown out. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.plate) .cap {
      position: absolute; left: 12px; bottom: 12px; z-index: 3;
      max-width: calc(100% - 24px);
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
      font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; font-size: 9.5px;
      letter-spacing: .10em; text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 7px 12px; border-radius: 999px;
    }
    /* .mat — stacked-print variant: a paper mat separating an overlapping inset
       photo from the plate beneath it. Dignifies a mediocre phone snap. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.plate).mat {
      border: 6px solid var(--paper);
      box-shadow: 0 22px 46px rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.22);
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BI"] :where(.plate) .ph { transition: none; } }

    /* ── .weave / .weave-i — rattan tooth. Apply ALONGSIDE background-color, never
          with the `background` shorthand (which would wipe the image layers). */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.weave) {
      background-image:
        repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.05) 0 1px, transparent 1px 7px),
        repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.04) 0 1px, transparent 1px 7px);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.weave-i) {
      background-image:
        repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.05) 0 1px, transparent 1px 7px),
        repeating-linear-gradient(-45deg, rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.04) 0 1px, transparent 1px 7px);
    }

    /* ── .sun — decorative sun arc. Always aria-hidden, always z-index 0. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.sun) {
      position: absolute; z-index: 0; pointer-events: none; border-radius: 50%;
      background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%,
        rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.22), rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.06) 58%, transparent 72%);
    }

    /* ── .slab — the raised woven panel (front-desk card, NAP card, CTA slab). */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.slab) {
      position: relative; background-color: var(--card);
      border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-lg);
      box-shadow: 0 20px 44px rgba(var(--ink-rgb),.12);
    }

    /* ── .chip — tinted meta chip. Ink glyph/label on an accent-TINTED field: the
          tint is the colour, the label is the contrast (9.71 on paper, 8.80 on card). */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.chip) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
      background-color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.16); color: var(--ink);
      border: 1px solid rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.42); border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 5px 11px;
      font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 500; font-size: 9.5px;
      letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .chip { color: var(--paper); border-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.28); }

    /* ── .rowrule — the one hairline row separator used by every list/ledger in the
          template. Per-cell border-top + auto-fit grids, deliberately NOT a
          gap-over-inked-container trick: that paints a visible block in the EMPTY
          tracks of a partial last row (5 amenities in a 4-col grid). */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.rowrule) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .rowrule { border-top-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb),.20); }

    /* ── .tick — the amenity/credential glyph. 34px rounded square, accent-tinted
          field, INK checkmark. No clip-art, no seal, no shield: a drawn badge is a
          visual claim of certification. */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.tick) {
      position: relative; display: block; width: 34px; height: 34px;
      border-radius: 11px; border: 1.5px solid var(--accent);
      background-color: rgba(var(--accent-rgb),.10);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.tick)::after {
      content: ""; position: absolute; left: 10px; top: 9px; width: 12px; height: 6px;
      border-left: 2px solid var(--ink); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
      transform: rotate(-45deg);
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.band-shade) .tick::after { border-color: var(--paper); }

    /* ── scroll reveal (PageBI's boot IIFE toggles .in) ───────────────── */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.reveal) { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(18px); transition: opacity .7s ease, transform .7s ease; }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.reveal.in) { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="1"]) { transition-delay: .08s; }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="2"]) { transition-delay: .16s; }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="3"]) { transition-delay: .24s; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page="BI"] .reveal { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; transition: none !important; }
    }

    /* ── skip link ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.skip) {
      position: absolute; left: -999px; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
      padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 0 0 var(--r-sm) 0;
      font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    html[data-page="BI"] :where(.skip:focus) { left: 0; top: 0; }

    /* ── SHARED MOBILE PASS · 760px ───────────────────────────────────── */
    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      html[data-page="BI"] section { padding: clamp(56px,11vw,80px) 0; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.wrap) { width: min(var(--maxw), 90vw); }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.h2) { font-size: clamp(28px,7.4vw,44px); max-width: none; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.lede) { max-width: none; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.sec-head) { font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: .14em; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.plate) { border-radius: var(--r-md); }
    }

    /* ── SHARED MOBILE PASS · 520px (verified no horizontal overflow at 360px) ── */
    @media (max-width: 520px) {
      html[data-page="BI"] body { font-size: 16px; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.h2) { font-size: clamp(26px,8.2vw,34px); letter-spacing: -.02em; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.kick) { font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .14em; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.btn) { padding: 14px 22px; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .12em; white-space: normal; text-align: center; flex: 1 1 100%; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.plate).mat { border-width: 4px; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.sec-head) { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 12px; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.sec-head) .sh-rule { order: 3; flex-basis: 100%; }
      html[data-page="BI"] :where(.sec-head) .sh-r { text-align: left; }
    }
  </style>

  {__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />}
  <style is:global set:html={__overrideCss}></style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <HeaderBI layout={layout} content={content} />
  <main id="main">
    {visibility.heroSection !== false && <HeroBI content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.trustBlock !== false && <TrustBI content={content} />}
    {/* Rooms → amenities → gallery lead, BEFORE the story: in this vertical the
        tariff and the photography are the product. Deliberate; do not reorder. */}
    {visibility.servicesSection !== false && <ServicesBI content={content} />}
    {visibility.whyUsBlock !== false && <WhyBI content={content} />}
    {visibility.gallerySection !== false && <GalleryBI content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.aboutSection !== false && <AboutBI content={content} />}
    {visibility.howItWorksBlock !== false && <HowBI content={content} />}
    {visibility.testimonialsBlock !== false && <TestimonialsBI content={content} />}
    {visibility.faqBlock !== false && <FaqBI content={content} />}
    {visibility.serviceAreaBlock !== false && <AreaBI content={content} />}
    {visibility.credentialsBlock !== false && <CredentialsBI content={content} />}
    {visibility.locationBlock !== false && <LocationBI content={content} layout={layout} />}
  </main>
  {visibility.ctaBandBlock !== false && <CtaBandBI content={content} layout={layout} />}
  <FooterBI layout={layout} content={content} />

  <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      if (!reduce && !document.hidden) {
        var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (es) {
          es.forEach(function (e) { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(e.target); } });
        }, { threshold: 0.1, rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px' });
        document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(function (el) { io.observe(el); });
      } else {
        document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(function (el) { el.classList.add('in'); });
      }
      // Palm Hour / BI Leaflet boot — accepts (lat, lng, label) from LocationBI.
      // The global name is family-unique on purpose: a preview harness can render
      // two wrappers in one document, and a shared name cross-wires the maps.
      window.__hospitalityBIInitMap = function (lat, lng, label) {
        if (!window.L) return;
        var el = document.getElementById('map'); if (!el) return;
        // Erases LocationBI's drawn fallback map-face; without this the tiles
        // stack on top of the gradient.
        el.innerHTML = '';
        var map = L.map('map', { scrollWheelZoom: false }).setView([lat, lng], 15);
        // LABELLED basemap: a guest orienting to a beach, pier or airport needs
        // place names, so this family uses CARTO voyager rather than nolabels.
        L.tileLayer('https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/rastertiles/voyager/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', { attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO', maxZoom: 19, subdomains: 'abcd' }).addTo(map);
        // Marker colours are READ from the live tokens rather than baked, so an
        // explicit admin colour pick recolours the pin too (buildOverrideCss sets
        // them on html:root, which is this same element).
        var cs = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
        var accent = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent') || '').trim() || '#BD5028';
        var paper = (cs.getPropertyValue('--paper') || '').trim() || '#F6EBDC';
        var icon = L.divIcon({
          className: '',
          html: '<div style="width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:' + accent + ';box-shadow:0 0 0 3px ' + paper + ';border:0;"></div>',
          iconSize: [16, 16], iconAnchor: [8, 8]
        });
        L.marker([lat, lng], { icon: icon }).addTo(map).bindPopup('<b>' + label + '</b>');
      };
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
